<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1166</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn was king of Ailech in the north of Ireland and, from 1156, high king of Ireland. The most powerful of the Mac Lochlainn kings of the Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>, he dominated the island for a decade and supported church reform, including the new Cistercian abbey of Mellifont. He was killed in 1166 after blinding a sworn ally, and Ruaidrí Ua Conchobair took the high kingship.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Mac Lochlainn line, notably <b>Muirchertach Mac Lochlainn</b>, held the high kingship in the 12th century.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-ailech">Kingdom of Ailech</a></li></ul></section>
